{"title":"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At Rachelle's school, an A counts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, a B <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, a C <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and a D <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Her GPA in the four classes she is taking is computed as the total sum of points divided by 4. She is certain that she will get A's in both Mathematics and Science and at least a C in each of English and History. She thinks she has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance of getting an A in English, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84a414e9655bf25b41aebc8c9f7bcb651acf2fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> chance of getting a B. In History, she has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance of getting an A, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance of getting a B, independently of what she gets in English. What is the probability that Rachelle will get a GPA of at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8245e043508c7c928c89b42f9ce38f04d720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/98405ba3ab5a03d5c0696c24f544e9d31e1631f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\; \\frac{11}{72} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\; \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\; \\frac{3}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\; \\frac{11}{24} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\; \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"392\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability that Rachelle gets a C in English is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadc914c9c7fd1d490c4f63392ddc67a2cb55602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The probability that she gets a C in History is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725d9353d6df8f64235c89f173f8fb1de49b9b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We see that the sum of Rachelle's \"point\" scores must be at least 14 since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0ca21f858e6a96158547b0219ebb6c3ded8c34a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4*3.5 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. We know that in Mathematics and Science we have a total point score of 8 (since she will get As in both), so we only need a sum of 6 in English and History. This can be achieved by getting two As, one A and one B, one A and one C, or two Bs. We evaluate these cases.\n</p><p>The probability that she gets two As is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30cf3959a24ee51024e10a8e3df51910ac43b2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The probability that she gets one A and one B is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098ad05cc91aa4f11e4cb2c9cfd5eecd8469ffa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{16} =  \\frac{8}{144}+\\frac{9}{144} = \\frac{17}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"354\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The probability that she gets one A and one C is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526d33ccec852dae6d47c9966dc103f866083f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{5}{12} + \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{5}{72}+\\frac{7}{48} =  \\frac{31}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"263\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The probability that she gets two Bs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/36897728b881d1e76e39a87685ea8cb1c7bd2f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Adding these, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/125c798d1b06a2bab6589fe0e0f4701cba2aeccf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{17}{144} +  \\frac{31}{144} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{66}{144} = \\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)}\\;  \\frac{11}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"322\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can break it up into three mutually exclusive cases: A in english, at least a C in history; B in english and at least a B in history; C in english and an A in history. This gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f359a821d376169b00ca63cfecb7adbadafdc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{6} \\cdot 1 + \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4}\\right) + \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\; \\frac{11}{24}}.\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Probability she gets a B in English and C in History is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/398ef7852223026082317c5982eb9a22854dfbd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{5}{12} = \\frac{5}{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Probability she gets a C in English and B in History is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8404b382b608e674a3180da6384885bcd244f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{7}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Probability she gets a C in English and C in History is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3cf9b9c1c43072dad05f8e8970972f6b4415e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} \\cdot \\frac{5}{12} = \\frac{35}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>In total, the probability she gets any of these cases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75038ec6a7d14f978911332461ed0609c513a257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{78}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25ec1d505184448e172e662bd2b273919faed3f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{78}{144} = \\frac{66}{144} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)},}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f226b6463f19a85c6b6e58b8dd72df1797f9a2ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~SirAppel\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Quick)\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rachelle is certain that she will get an A in Math and Science. She will also get at least a C in both History and English. This means that her baseline GPA is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We make the observation that if she gets either an A in History or an A in English she will get a GPA of at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8245e043508c7c928c89b42f9ce38f04d720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. However, she can also get a B in history and a B in English and still get a GPA of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8245e043508c7c928c89b42f9ce38f04d720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The probability that Rachelle gets an A in either History or English is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92aaa0948641956d161e952fe1e083c261263ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac {5}{6} \\cdot \\frac {3}{4} = \\frac {3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" />. The probability that Rachelle gets a B in both History an English is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72c67797d7c78afe7fcb612ba4158c304c896f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{3} \\cdot \\frac {1}{4} = \\frac {1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />. Summing the two gets the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42b38e152c0dfd132f6fcac15e5848775679344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D)} \\frac {11}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"65\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B\">2015 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235957\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 258/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6569/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.969      1 -total\n 57.93%    8.092      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.39%    5.502      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14017:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235957 and revision id 205196. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}